  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3159fa09",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2  Define the Churn Label (Leakage-Safe)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Protocol — same as the Olist notebook, for direct comparability:**\n",
    "- **Observation window**: `T − 365 days` → `T`\n",
    "- **Prediction window**: `T` → `T + 180 days`\n",
    "- **Churn label = 1** if customer makes zero bookings in the prediction window, else 0\n",
    "- Features computed **only** on the observation window — no leakage\n",
    "- **Modelling population restricted to repeat customers (≥2 bookings in the observation window)** — same restriction as Olist, kept for methodological consistency across the report, even though this dataset is much less affected by the one-time-buyer problem.\n",
    "\n",
    "Cutoff is chosen so the full 180-day prediction window stays inside the dataset's date range (same right-censoring logic as the Olist fix)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "aa286f9e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Full data range: 2009-12-01 → 2011-12-09\n",
      "\n",
      "Observation window : 2010-06-12 → 2011-06-12\n",
      "Prediction window  : 2011-06-12 → 2011-12-09\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "data_max_date = bookings['booking_date'].max()\n",
    "data_min_date = bookings['booking_date'].min()\n",
    "print(f'Full data range: {data_min_date.date()} → {data_max_date.date()}')\n",
    "\n",
    "CHURN_DAYS  = 180\n",
    "MIN_BOOKINGS = 2\n",
    "\n",
    "# cutoff = (latest date) - 180 days, so the prediction window fits exactly\n",
    "# inside the data, then back off a further 365 days for the observation window\n",
    "CUTOFF    = (data_max_date - pd.DateOffset(days=CHURN_DAYS)).normalize()\n",
    "OBS_START = CUTOFF - pd.DateOffset(days=365)\n",
    "PRED_END  = CUTOFF + pd.DateOffset(days=CHURN_DAYS)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\nObservation window : {OBS_START.date()} → {CUTOFF.date()}')\n",
    "print(f'Prediction window  : {CUTOFF.date()} → {PRED_END.date()}')\n",
    "\n",
    "if OBS_START < data_min_date:\n",
    "    print(f'\\n⚠ WARNING: observation window starts before the data begins '\n",
    "          f'({OBS_START.date()} < {data_min_date.date()}). Some customers\\' '\n",
    "          f'full 365-day history will be truncated. Consider this in §3.3 if it occurs.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "03933d87",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Customers in obs window (all)      : 4,365\n",
      "Customers with >=2 bookings (kept) : 3,027\n",
      "One-time buyers excluded            : 1,338 (30.7% of obs-window customers)\n",
      "\n",
      "Active customers in obs window (repeat-only) : 3,027\n",
      "Churn rate                                   : 31.4%  (label=1 → no return within 180 days)\n",
      "Non-churned (minority class) count           : 2,076\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# bookings in observation window (features come from here)\n",
    "obs_all = bookings[(bookings['booking_date'] >= OBS_START) &\n",
    "                   (bookings['booking_date'] <  CUTOFF)].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── restrict to repeat customers (>=2 bookings in obs window) ──────────────\n",
    "booking_counts = obs_all.groupby('customer_id')['booking_id'].count()\n",
    "repeat_customers = booking_counts[booking_counts >= MIN_BOOKINGS].index\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Customers in obs window (all)      : {obs_all[\"customer_id\"].nunique():,}')\n",
    "print(f'Customers with >=2 bookings (kept) : {len(repeat_customers):,}')\n",
    "print(f'One-time buyers excluded            : {obs_all[\"customer_id\"].nunique() - len(repeat_customers):,} '\n",
    "      f'({(1 - len(repeat_customers)/obs_all[\"customer_id\"].nunique()):.1%} of obs-window customers)')\n",
    "\n",
    "obs = obs_all[obs_all['customer_id'].isin(repeat_customers)].copy()\n",
    "active_customers = obs['customer_id'].unique()\n",
    "\n",
    "# bookings in prediction window (label comes from here)\n",
    "pred = bookings[(bookings['booking_date'] >= CUTOFF) &\n",
    "                (bookings['booking_date'] <  PRED_END)].copy()\n",
    "returned = set(pred['customer_id'].unique())\n",
    "\n",
    "labels = pd.DataFrame({'customer_id': active_customers})\n",
    "labels['churned'] = (~labels['customer_id'].isin(returned)).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "churn_rate = labels['churned'].mean()\n",
    "print(f'\\nActive customers in obs window (repeat-only) : {len(labels):,}')\n",
    "print(f'Churn rate                                   : {churn_rate:.1%}  (label=1 → no return within {CHURN_DAYS} days)')\n",
    "print(f'Non-churned (minority class) count           : {(labels[\"churned\"]==0).sum():,}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "af622f06",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Sanity check before proceeding:** if the non-churned minority class count above is still under ~100, the same sample-size ceiling diagnosed for Olist will likely recur here too. Online Retail II's repeat-purchase density is substantially higher than Olist's, so this is expected to pass, but it's worth confirming before trusting any downstream model comparison."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8bf70681",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3  Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "Same feature families as the Olist notebook, **minus the location feature** (no coordinates in this dataset):\n",
    "\n",
    "- **`feat_rfm`** — Recency, Frequency, Monetary only (Logistic Regression baseline)\n",
    "- **`feat_ext`** — Full extended set (RF + XGBoost candidate), including spend-volatility (`spend_per_visit_std`/`cv`) but **not** `dist_from_centroid_km`\n",
    "\n",
    "All features computed strictly on the observation window."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "b7a50982",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Feature matrix shape: (3027, 18)\n",
      "Missing values:\n",
      "inter_booking_gap_std    808\n",
      "dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "grp = obs.groupby('customer_id')\n",
    "\n",
    "feat = pd.DataFrame(index=labels.set_index('customer_id').index)\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- RECENCY ---\n",
    "last_booking  = grp['booking_date'].max()\n",
    "first_booking = grp['booking_date'].min()\n",
    "feat['recency_days'] = (CUTOFF - last_booking).dt.days\n",
    "feat['tenure_days']  = (CUTOFF - first_booking).dt.days\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- FREQUENCY ---\n",
    "feat['freq_12m'] = grp['booking_id'].count()\n",
    "\n",
    "obs_3m = obs[obs['booking_date'] >= (CUTOFF - pd.DateOffset(days=90))]\n",
    "freq_3m = obs_3m.groupby('customer_id')['booking_id'].count()\n",
    "feat['freq_3m'] = freq_3m.reindex(feat.index).fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "def inter_gap_stats(dates):\n",
    "    if len(dates) < 2:\n",
    "        return pd.Series({'gap_mean': np.nan, 'gap_std': np.nan})\n",
    "    gaps = dates.sort_values().diff().dt.days.dropna()\n",
    "    return pd.Series({'gap_mean': gaps.mean(), 'gap_std': gaps.std()})\n",
    "\n",
    "gap_stats = grp['booking_date'].apply(inter_gap_stats).unstack()\n",
    "feat['avg_inter_booking_gap'] = gap_stats['gap_mean']\n",
    "feat['inter_booking_gap_std'] = gap_stats['gap_std']\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- MONETARY ---\n",
    "feat['total_spend_12m'] = grp['invoice_amount'].sum()\n",
    "feat['avg_ticket']      = grp['invoice_amount'].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "def spend_trend(amounts):\n",
    "    if len(amounts) < 2:\n",
    "        return 0.0\n",
    "    x = np.arange(len(amounts[-6:]))\n",
    "    y = amounts.sort_index().values[-6:]\n",
    "    return np.polyfit(x, y, 1)[0] if len(x) > 1 else 0.0\n",
    "\n",
    "feat['monetary_trend'] = grp['invoice_amount'].apply(spend_trend)\n",
    "\n",
    "# spend-per-visit volatility (same rationale as Olist notebook)\n",
    "feat['spend_per_visit_std'] = grp['invoice_amount'].std()\n",
    "feat['spend_per_visit_cv']  = feat['spend_per_visit_std'] / feat['avg_ticket']\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- ENGAGEMENT ---\n",
    "feat['cancellation_rate'] = grp['cancelled'].mean()\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- DIVERSITY ---\n",
    "feat['unique_item_types'] = grp['item_count'].mean()   # avg distinct SKUs per basket\n",
    "feat['total_units']       = grp['unit_count'].sum()\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- CALENDAR ---\n",
    "feat['weekend_share'] = grp['booking_date'].apply(lambda d: (d.dt.dayofweek >= 5).mean())\n",
    "feat['evening_share'] = grp['booking_date'].apply(lambda d: (d.dt.hour >= 17).mean())\n",
    "\n",
    "# --- GEOGRAPHY (categorical, not coordinate-based) ---\n",
    "# No lat/lng available in this dataset. Country is retained as a coarse proxy —\n",
    "# encoded as a binary 'is_domestic' flag (UK vs. non-UK) since the customer base\n",
    "# is overwhelmingly UK-based and this avoids a high-cardinality categorical.\n",
    "customer_country = grp['country'].first()\n",
    "feat['is_uk'] = (customer_country == 'United Kingdom').astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── merge labels ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "feat = feat.merge(labels.set_index('customer_id')[['churned']],\n",
    "                  left_index=True, right_index=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Feature matrix shape: {feat.shape}')\n",
    "print(f'Missing values:\\n{feat.isnull().sum()[feat.isnull().sum()>0]}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "e37311a6",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "RFM feature set (3 features): ['recency_days', 'freq_12m', 'total_spend_12m']\n",
      "Extended feature set (17 features): ['recency_days', 'tenure_days', 'freq_12m', 'freq_3m', 'avg_inter_booking_gap', 'inter_booking_gap_std', 'total_spend_12m', 'avg_ticket', 'monetary_trend', 'spend_per_visit_std', 'spend_per_visit_cv', 'cancellation_rate', 'unique_item_types', 'total_units', 'weekend_share', 'evening_share', 'is_uk']\n",
      "Target distribution: 31.4% churn (class=1), n=3,027\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "RFM_FEATURES = ['recency_days', 'freq_12m', 'total_spend_12m']\n",
    "\n",
    "EXT_FEATURES = [\n",
    "    'recency_days', 'tenure_days',\n",
    "    'freq_12m', 'freq_3m',\n",
    "    'avg_inter_booking_gap', 'inter_booking_gap_std',\n",
    "    'total_spend_12m', 'avg_ticket', 'monetary_trend',\n",
    "    'spend_per_visit_std', 'spend_per_visit_cv',\n",
    "    'cancellation_rate',\n",
    "    'unique_item_types', 'total_units',\n",
    "    'weekend_share', 'evening_share',\n",
    "    'is_uk',\n",
    "]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Clear out the infinities globally\n",
    "feat = feat.replace([np.inf, -np.inf], np.nan)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Extract RAW arrays containing NaNs (Notice we REMOVED SimpleImputer from here)\n",
    "y = feat['churned'].values\n",
    "X_rfm = feat[RFM_FEATURES].values\n",
    "X_ext = feat[EXT_FEATURES].values\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'RFM feature set ({len(RFM_FEATURES)} features): {RFM_FEATURES}')\n",
    "print(f'Extended feature set ({len(EXT_FEATURES)} features): {EXT_FEATURES}')\n",
    "print(f'Target distribution: {y.mean():.1%} churn (class=1), n={len(y):,}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1c5327ba",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4  Train / Test Split + SMOTE\n",
    "\n",
    "- Stratified 80/20 split to preserve class ratio\n",
    "- SMOTE applied **only to training set**\n",
    "- Cite: Chawla et al. (2002)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "id": "4484126b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "ename": "ModuleNotFoundError",
     "evalue": "No module named 'imblearn'",
     "output_type": "error",
     "traceback": [
      "\u001b[31m---------------------------------------------------------------------------\u001b[39m",
      "\u001b[31mModuleNotFoundError\u001b[39m                       Traceback (most recent call last)",
      "\u001b[36mCell\u001b[39m\u001b[36m \u001b[39m\u001b[32mIn[13]\u001b[39m\u001b[32m, line 3\u001b[39m\n\u001b[32m      1\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;28;01mfrom\u001b[39;00m sklearn.model_selection \u001b[38;5;28;01mimport\u001b[39;00m train_test_split\n\u001b[32m      2\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;28;01mfrom\u001b[39;00m sklearn.impute \u001b[38;5;28;01mimport\u001b[39;00m SimpleImputer\n\u001b[32m----> \u001b[39m\u001b[32m3\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;28;01mfrom\u001b[39;00m imblearn.over_sampling \u001b[38;5;28;01mimport\u001b[39;00m SMOTE\n\u001b[32m      4\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;28;01mimport\u001b[39;00m numpy \u001b[38;5;28;01mas\u001b[39;00m np\n\u001b[32m      5\u001b[39m \n\u001b[32m      6\u001b[39m \u001b[38;5;66;03m# 1. Generate stratified split indices\u001b[39;00m\n",
      "\u001b[31mModuleNotFoundError\u001b[39m: No module named 'imblearn'"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n",
    "from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n",
    "from imblearn.over_sampling import SMOTE\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Generate stratified split indices\n",
    "idx = np.arange(len(y))\n",
    "idx_train, idx_test = train_test_split(idx, test_size=0.2,\n",
    "                                       stratify=y,\n",
    "                                       random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Extract RAW data slices (assumes X_rfm and X_ext have NOT been imputed yet)\n",
    "X_rfm_train_raw, X_rfm_test_raw = X_rfm[idx_train], X_rfm[idx_test]\n",
    "X_ext_train_raw, X_ext_test_raw = X_ext[idx_train], X_ext[idx_test]\n",
    "y_train, y_test                 = y[idx_train], y[idx_test]\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. CRITICAL FIX: Fit imputer ONLY on train data, then transform test data\n",
    "imp_rfm = SimpleImputer(strategy='median')\n",
    "X_rfm_train = imp_rfm.fit_transform(X_rfm_train_raw)\n",
    "X_rfm_test  = imp_rfm.transform(X_rfm_test_raw)\n",
    "\n",
    "imp_ext = SimpleImputer(strategy='median')\n",
    "X_ext_train = imp_ext.fit_transform(X_ext_train_raw)\n",
    "X_ext_test  = imp_ext.transform(X_ext_test_raw)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 4. Apply SMOTE exclusively to the cleanly imputed training data\n",
    "sm = SMOTE(random_state=RANDOM_STATE)\n",
    "X_rfm_train_res, y_train_res_rfm = sm.fit_resample(X_rfm_train, y_train)\n",
    "X_ext_train_res, y_train_res_ext = sm.fit_resample(X_ext_train, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Metrics Verification ──────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "print(f'Train size (before SMOTE): {len(y_train):,}  (churn rate {y_train.mean():.1%})')\n",
    "print(f'Train size (after SMOTE) : {len(y_train_res_rfm):,} (RFM) / {len(y_train_res_ext):,} (ext)')\n",
    "print(f'Test size                : {len(y_test):,}  (churn rate {y_test.mean():.1%})')\n",
    "print(f'\\nMinority class in training set before SMOTE: {(y_train==1).sum():,} examples')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5ed0dd74",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5  Evaluation Harness\n",
    "\n",
    "Same metrics as the Olist notebook, for direct comparability:\n",
    "- **PR-AUC** — primary metric for imbalanced binary classification\n",
    "- **ROC-AUC** — prevalence-invariant; the more honest comparator when the base rate is itself extreme\n",
    "- **F1-score**\n",
    "- **Brier Score** — calibration quality for the High/Medium/Low UI risk buckets"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 14,
   "id": "404168c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Evaluation harness ready ✓\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.metrics import (\n",
    "    roc_auc_score, average_precision_score,\n",
    "    f1_score, brier_score_loss,\n",
    "    precision_recall_curve, roc_curve\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "results = []\n",
    "\n",
    "def evaluate(name, model, X_test, y_test, feature_set_label):\n",
    "    y_prob = model.predict_proba(X_test)[:, 1]\n",
    "    y_pred = (y_prob >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
    "\n",
    "    pr_auc  = average_precision_score(y_test, y_prob)\n",
    "    roc_auc = roc_auc_score(y_test, y_prob)\n",
    "    f1      = f1_score(y_test, y_pred)\n",
    "    brier   = brier_score_loss(y_test, y_prob)\n",
    "\n",
    "    results.append({\n",
    "        'Model':       name,\n",
    "        'Features':    feature_set_label,\n",
    "        'PR-AUC':      round(pr_auc,  4),\n",
    "        'ROC-AUC':     round(roc_auc, 4),\n",
    "        'F1':          round(f1,      4),\n",
    "        'Brier Score': round(brier,   4),\n",
    "        '_y_prob':     y_prob,\n",
    "    })\n",
    "\n",
    "    print(f'\\n── {name} ({feature_set_label}) ──')\n",
    "    print(f'  PR-AUC  : {pr_auc:.4f}')\n",
    "    print(f'  ROC-AUC : {roc_auc:.4f}')\n",
    "    print(f'  F1      : {f1:.4f}')\n",
    "    print(f'  Brier   : {brier:.4f}')\n",
    "    return model\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Evaluation harness ready ✓')"
   ]
  },
