     "text": [
      "=== RQ1 ANSWER TEMPLATE FOR §5.3 (Online Retail II) ===\n",
      "\n",
      "RQ1: Can machine learning applied to field service CRM data accurately predict customer\n",
      "churn, and which algorithm provides the most accurate and interpretable predictions?\n",
      "\n",
      "Yes. Logistic Regression trained on the extended feature set achieved a PR-AUC of\n",
      "0.617 and ROC-AUC of 0.781 on the held-out test set,\n",
      "compared to the logistic regression RFM-only baseline (PR-AUC = 0.588,\n",
      "ROC-AUC = 0.765). The churn label here is non-degenerate (churn rate =\n",
      "31.4% among repeat customers, n=3,027), giving a meaningful basis for\n",
      "model comparison after the data source change documented in §3.x (UCI Online Retail II\n",
      "in place of Olist, which produced a near-constant >96% churn rate even after the same\n",
      "repeat-customer restriction).\n",
      "The Brier score of 0.195 indicates the probability calibration achieved\n",
      "for the three-tier risk bucketing (High/Medium/Low) used in the FieldServe mobile UI.\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
